WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
In the Bhagavad Gita,
Krishna traces a chain.

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.000
It starts small: dwelling
on things you want.

3
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.300
Attraction grows into desire.

4
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.000
Desire flames into passion.

5
00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.210
Step by step, the mind is undone.

6
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:19.100
Many Hindus believe past
actions, even from past lives,

7
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:21.660
set the situation you are born into.

8
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:26.210
So if your past shapes your
life now, are you still free?

9
00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.910
And how should you treat
someone who suffers?

10
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.650
In this mission, you'll explore
Hindu ideas about free will,

11
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.890
ignorance and the true self.

12
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:39.760
Then you'll weigh up a hard claim: is all
suffering the result of a person's own

13
00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.890
karma?

14
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:44.470
Your mission: find out
how free karma leaves you,

15
00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.680
and how Hindus respond to suffering.
